WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.105
Module 3 focused on retrieving filtering and
changing individual rows Module

00:00:06.132 --> 00:00:11.000
4 changes the perspective Instead of asking which
records should I return

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:14.368
we often ask questions such as how many how much
what is

00:00:14.395 --> 00:00:19.900
the average or which group is largest A good
aggregation starts with

00:00:19.926 --> 00:00:24.495
the business question Then we define the output
grain choose the measures

00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:29.468
apply row-level filters apply group-level filters
when needed and finally validate the

00:00:29.482 --> 00:00:34.982
result A simple way to think about it is detail
grain measure

00:00:35.153 --> 00:00:39.813
filter and validate If the final summary does not
match the meaning

00:00:39.827 --> 00:00:44.129
of the question even perfectly valid SQL can produce
a misleading answer
